    "id": "news-1787401177093-1",
    "title": "Puntland Condemns Civilian Deaths in Coastal Airstrike Near Garmaal",
    "original_title": "Puntland condemns reported Turkish airstrike that killed 4 civilian fishermen in Garmaal",
    "slug": "puntland-condemns-civilian-deaths-in-coastal-airstrike-near-garmaal",
    "summary": "Puntland authorities have condemned an airstrike near Garmaal that killed four fishermen and wounded two others, warning that such incidents could undermine cooperation with international partners in the fight against piracy.",
    "content": "Authorities in Somalia's semi-autonomous Puntland region have publicly condemned an airstrike that took place near the coastal town of Garmaal, resulting in the deaths of four people and injuries to two others. The Puntland Ministry of Security issued a statement on Friday identifying the victims as civilian fishermen and expressing strong opposition to military actions by international forces that affect civilians and their property.\n\nThe incident occurred along Somalia's northeastern coast, an area that has been a focus for international naval operations against piracy. Puntland officials have warned that such attacks on civilians could seriously damage the working relationship between its own security agencies and international partners, who have collaborated closely in anti-piracy efforts.\n\nThe ministry's statement stressed that strikes against civilian targets are unacceptable and could hinder future cooperation, which is vital for maintaining regional security. This event highlights ongoing tensions between counter-piracy operations and the protection of local livelihoods.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, many of whom have ties to Puntland, this news raises concerns about the safety of family members and the stability of the region. The incident also underscores the risks faced by coastal communities who depend on fishing, a key economic activity that is now threatened by such military actions.\n\nAs investigations into the airstrike are expected to unfold, Puntland authorities are calling for greater caution to prevent further civilian casualties. The balance between international security operations and the rights of local civilians remains a critical issue, with implications for diaspora confidence and regional development.\n\nRead the original report from Somalia Guardian here: https://www.somaliguardian.com/news/somalia-news/puntland-condemns-reported-turkish-airstrike-killed-4-civilian-fishermen-garmaal/",
    "source": "somaliguardian.com",
    "source_name": "Somalia Guardian",
    "original_url": "https://www.somaliguardian.com/news/somalia-news/puntland-condemns-reported-turkish-airstrike-killed-4-civilian-fishermen-garmaal/",
